PREFIX : <https://arco.ai/ontology/core#>
PREFIX iao: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>

# AUDIT LAYER ONLY — flag, not classification.
#
# Returns TRUE when a provider has submitted a DerogationClaim artifact
# that is_about the system under evaluation.
#
# A DerogationClaim is a provider-asserted ICE (cco:DescriptiveInformationContentEntity)
# representing a claim that the system qualifies for the Article 6(3) derogation:
# "shall not be considered to be high-risk where it does not pose a significant risk
# of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons."
#
# This query does NOT evaluate whether the derogation applies. It only detects
# that a claim artifact exists in the documentary record. If TRUE, the certificate
# emits FLAGGED and directs human legal review before treating the OWL classification
# as a final legal determination.
#
# OWL classification is UNCHANGED by this flag. The flag fires after OWL-RL
# reasoning is complete and does not affect any gate condition.
#
# The pipeline binds ?system to the actual system IRI via initBindings
# when --system is provided.

ASK WHERE {
  ?claim rdf:type :DerogationClaim ;
         iao:0000136 ?system .
}
